# Server-managed copy

When deciding where user-facing text belongs, use this test:

- **Would this text need to change when the service behavior changes, without an app release?**
  - If yes: serve it from the API (`GET /managed-copy/:slug`).
  - If no: keep it in the i18n catalog.

Most UI copy stays in the catalog. Served copy is for operational content that can change between
releases.

## Current served documents

- About (`about`)
- FAQ (`faq`)
- Make Clip how-to (`clip-how-to`)
- Developer (`developer`)

## App link tokens

A markdown link can name a destination without a host. The surface resolves the token.

- `[label]({{api_reference}})` — interactive API docs for this server
- `[label]({{api_spec}})` — raw OpenAPI document for this server
- `[label]({{settings_developer}})` — Settings, Developer tab

Any other `{{…}}` href stays plain text.

A described link is the bordered title-and-sentence card (`DescribedLink` on web). The first line
is the title. The following lines are the sentence. The key names the same destinations:

```markdown
{{described_link:api_reference}}
API Reference
Opens the interactive API reference served by this server.
{{/described_link}}
```

## Legal documents

Terms of Service stay a versioned acceptance document on `GET /legal/terms` (public). The response
is a short intro plus the full markdown for the configured terms version, and it shows an
agreement date. The account accepts or declines that version.

The Taste Profile agreement stays on `GET /legal/taste-profile-agreement` (authenticated), not a
managed-copy slug, because the explanation can change without an app release. That document
explains the feature. It is not the legal notice and it does not show an agreement date. The
legal notice is the terms.

The server version still gates tracking. Bump it only when what is recorded, how long it is kept,
or who can see it changes. A wording change that leaves those the same does not bump the version.

Do not add a `terms` or `taste-profile-agreement` managed-copy slug, and do not fold either document
into `GET /managed-copy/:slug`.

## Rules

- Do not add bundled fallback prose for served documents in app code or locale JSON.
- Always render loading and retry states while fetching served documents.
- Add new managed-copy docs by adding locale markdown files plus allowlisted slug support, not by
  creating a new endpoint for each document. Terms of Service and the Taste Profile agreement
  stay on `/legal/*`.

